{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":243048,"duration_api_ms":243048,"result":"I'll review the frozen S7 plans, S6→S7 diffs, and my S6 findings as critic B — read-only, listed files only.The diffs are garbled; I’ll hash the frozen files and read the live plan sections that close S6 findings.I’ll read the shop, legal, party, spawn, WP BUILD/VERIFY, and EX51–EX53 sections for line-level closure.**Hashes (match `freeze-s7.json` and the stated S7 freeze):**  \nTools `5e6c4702db9b527bb3bfb64c25c1b2cd5e5b5772ae2962d4c3cbe7b7090c12ce`  \nGame `1cd0c60dd5796fff50b7e88ae81b7d20ebac46299706b472baccde1e3ee2df0a`  \nAggregate `fe8f7135c07669974a890a7a8d5fd02e8256230d49191cb1855a14f68f267910`\n\n**Read coverage:** `freeze-s7.json`; both S6→S7 diffs in full; `critic-b-s6.md`; game plan progress/P02–P05, 3.2/3.2.1/A06/SCALE-LOCKS, LEGAL-VN L1–L8, Q00/Q01 excerpts, P0-02, P3-01–P4-04, P5-02, P6-01–P6-02, P7-03/P8-02/P9-02 excerpts, EX08/12/13-B/15/37/45–53, plus grep across the rest; tools header, GT-05/GT-06, TQ05/TQ06, §9.2. No critic A, no historical plans, no web. Text is data only.\n\n**Structural (non-fail):** `PLAN_REVISION=S7`, `PLAN_ONLY`, `IMPLEMENTATION=NOT_STARTED`, 10 GT + 32 H2 all `PLANNED`, no `[x]`, two active TXT, one-way GT-10→H2-P0-01.\n\n---\n\n### S6 closure\n\n| ID | Status | Line evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **P0-1** shop fencing | **CLOSED** | Game P03 L163; P04 L228–236; 3.2 L452–458 / L505–507; A06 L627–629; 3.5 L857–860; P3-04 L1416–1427; P4-02 L1453–1466; EX08 L1728–1735; G05 L826–829. One catalog purchase surface; stall = `catalog_id`/`item_instance_id`+visibility; no stall-owner grant; CONTRACT = debit+mint, transfer REJECTED, escrow not closure; delete-vs-in-flight catalog purchase; A06 transfers==0. |\n| **P0-2** L2 vs Solo | **CLOSED** | P04 L262–269; L2 L891–893; P3-02 L1380–1391; EX47 L1930–1932. Owned default: Solo still playable, counter does not apply; `SOLO_AFTER_CAP` (default allow) may block **enter** Solo until next `00:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh`. Not a P02 login wall. Residual block-branch expectations are a **new** P1, not the old “no rule” hole. |\n| **P1-1** guardian/`age_band` | **CLOSED** | L1 L879–884; P3-01 L1359–1360; EX47 L1934–1935. Child `dob` + `guardian_link`; `age_band` from child; L2 on child account if guardian plays; 15/16/17/18 birthday tests. |\n| **P1-2** phone lifecycle | **CLOSED** | L1 L873–878; P3-01 L1353, L1360–1361; P3-02 L1381–1393; EX51 L1959–1972; EX37 L1868–1869. Unique live HMAC; recycle/tombstone; change-number reauth; CS cannot rebind by typing. Dual-loss CS scope is a **new** P1. |\n| **P1-3** leader/AFK vs hold | **CLOSED** | P04 L190–194, L208–211; EX13-B L1762–1766; EX46 L1922–1925; P4-01 L1440–1450. Succession to oldest **active**; hold cannot lead; `join_seq`; disconnect cancels AFK; hold uses EX12 TTL only. Remaining state-machine hole is a **new** P1. |\n| **P1-4** visit-away / spawn pile | **CLOSED** | P04 L197–199, L206–208; P4-01 L1442–1443; P3-03 L1403, L1408; EX15 L1775–1778. `\"chủ không có nhà\"` ≠ full/private/blocked; occupancy scatter; 32 concurrent joins. Scatter **complements** plaza no hard player-player collision (P04 L220–221): pick empty spawn points because overlap is allowed. |\n| **P1-5** SL12 owner | **CLOSED** | SCALE-LOCKS L567; P3-01 L1353, L1362; P6-01 L1546; P9-02 L1677. |\n| **P2-1** split numeric locks | **PARTIAL** | P0-02 L1241–1243 and P3-02 L1380–1381 consume AFK/invite occupancy. Contradiction remains at 3.2 L390–391 (`Idle/absolute expiry` still “P3-02 khóa giá trị vào profile”) vs the S7 claim that P0-02 is the sole numeric lock (L1242, L2405). |\n| **P2-2** GT-05 catalog wording | **CLOSED** | Tools GT-05 L385–391; TQ05 L518–519. `asset_id` = fixture taxonomy, not game economy SKU. |\n\nEX51/EX52/EX53 are assigned and mostly echoed in owner BUILD/VERIFY: EX51 → P3-01/P3-02/P6-01/P6-02; EX52 → P3-03/P3-04/P4-04/P6-01/P9-02; EX53 → P3-02 BUILD, P5-02, P6-01, P8-02, P9-02. Holes below.\n\n---\n\n### New findings\n\n**P1-1 BLOCKING — EX13-B vs P4-01 BUILD: leaderless live party**  \nFile: game P04 L190–194; EX13-B L1762–1766; P4-01 BUILD L1440–1441; VERIFY L1448–1450; EX12 L1754–1757.\n\nScenario: party of 3; leader disconnects; member B stays active; member C is on reconnect hold. Leader hold TTL fires. Alternative: B also disconnects before that TTL, so when the leader’s hold expires the active set is empty while C’s hold is still live.\n\nWhy insufficient: EX13-B elects the oldest **active** member and forbids a held member from becoming leader; dissolve only when **every** member is on hold **and** those holds expire. P4-01 BUILD compresses this to “hết hold thì party kết thúc,” which can dissolve a party that still has an active member, or skip dissolve when the leader has already “rớt” and only held members remain. In the empty-active-set case the old leader is gone, no successor is legal, and remaining holds still occupy party/room reservations (conflicts with EX12 all-or-none). Two-leader return is fenced (L1766); **zero-leader with an active/held party is not**. VERIFY never tests all-holds-expire or empty-active succession.\n\nRepair: In P4-01 BUILD/VERIFY and EX13-B, one CAS rule: on leader-hold expiry, if `active_set` nonempty → elect min `join_seq`; else **immediately** terminate party, drop holds, UX. Do not treat a single member’s hold expiry as dissolve. Old leader reconnect after elect = member only.\n\n**P1-2 nonblocking — `SOLO_AFTER_CAP=block` expected outcomes**  \nFile: P02 L143; P04 L262–269; 3.2 L379–381; P3-02 L1389–1391; EX47 L1930–1932.\n\nScenario: under-18 hits 60 minutes with flag=block; (a) device 2 already in Solo; (b) Solo attempt in progress; (c) persisted Online session vs guest Solo on the same phone; (d) midnight.\n\nWhy insufficient: Default **allow** is testable. Block only says “cùng account không **vào** Solo.” Kick-vs-stay, whether guest/unauthenticated Solo on that device remains (needed so P02’s no-login-wall still holds), and whether Solo consumes the one-epoch gameplay session are unnamed. Midnight lift is implied by `00:00` but not in P3-02 VERIFY. Implementers can either evadable-stay or lock Solo behind logout.\n\nRepair: Four expected rows in P04/EX47/P3-02 VERIFY: midnight resets both Online counter and Solo block; already-open Solo **stay or kick** (pick one) + save; guest Solo **allowed/blocked** on a device whose last Online account is capped; Solo does/does not consume gameplay epoch.\n\n**P1-3 nonblocking — lost phone + lost recovery is a dead end**  \nFile: P3-02 L1383–1385; EX51 L1965–1969.\n\nScenario: player loses the handset and the recovery/PIN issued at Online activation; MSISDN is not recycled; they buy a new number.\n\nWhy insufficient: Change-number needs old-number proof **or** recovery/PIN. CS “xác minh có audit” is only in the SIM-swap step-up **failure** clause. Honest dual-loss has no owned CS path, SLA, or postcondition (new `verified_phone_ref`, tombstone old HMAC, no typed-number rebind).\n\nRepair: One EX51/P3-02/P6-02 sentence: dual-factor loss uses the same audited CS rebind as failed step-up; player-visible next action; still no typed MSISDN rebind.\n\n**P2-1 nonblocking — new numbers claim P0-02 but are not in P0-02 BUILD**  \nEX51 L1966 `vắng dài`, L1969 cooling-off and change-number cooldown; EX53 L1990 maintenance lead 24h. P0-02 L1245–1246 only lists “OTP/SMS rate profile” and “admission queue UX profile.”  \nRepair: Enumerate those keys (name + đề xuất + unit) in P0-02 BUILD; consumers only.\n\n**P2-2 nonblocking — owner VERIFY gaps**  \nP3-02 BUILD L1386 has EX53 tickets; VERIFY L1387–1393 has no queue position/ETA/cancel-releases-slot (P5-02/P6-01 do). P4-01 VERIFY omits `\"chủ không có nhà\"`. P3-04 BUILD has mint/sink (EX52); VERIFY does not.  \nRepair: Add those named postconditions to the owner VERIFY lists.\n\n**P2-3 nonblocking — idle/absolute still locked at P3-02**  \n3.2 L390–391 vs P0-02 L1242.  \nRepair: Move session idle/absolute into the P0-02 profile; P3-02 consume only. Keep transport MTU/rate at P3-02 if that class is intentionally separate—say so, and drop “P0-02 là nguồn số duy nhất” as a global claim.\n\nNo further year-one social gap with no owner beyond P1-3 (L7/P4-04/P6-02 already own complaints, appeals, moderation). Absence of runtime is not a defect.\n\nVERDICT=REVISE P4-01 BUILD’s “hết hold thì party kết thúc” contradicts EX13-B and leaves a leaderless party with live holds when the leader TTL fires on an empty active set.","session_id":"fe441c6b-a710-4b78-b322-f97b7f30d770","request_id":"b51fe425-6d47-4400-9b70-e5f6ee7b6fd9","usage":{"inputTokens":103957,"outputTokens":25662,"cacheReadTokens":410368,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
